					text2 = "Socialist traditions";
					text = "Nexhmije Hoxha has long been visited by various religious figures, mostly imams, because friendly relations have been established between the authorities and religion. Some particularly perspicacious Party members noticed that the ancient caliphates and socialism have much in common. Institutions such as social assistance to the poor and pensions were introduced in the early Shari'ah law in the form of «zakat», as one of the Five Pillars of Islam, in the Arab Caliphate in the 7th century. Taxes (in particular, zakat or jizya) were collected by the treasury of the Islamic government and used to provide assistance to the needy, including the poor, the elderly, orphans, widows and the disabled. According to the Islamic jurist and philosopher Al-Ghazali (1058-1111), the government also made food supplies in every region of the country in case of a natural disaster or famine. A caliphate can thus be considered the world's first welfare state and a social state. Perhaps we ourselves should focus on this?";
